AWS IAM – Real-Time Scenario Based Questions (Most Important Topics)
👉 If you’re preparing for AWS interviews or want to strengthen your IAM skills, these scenario-based questions will help sharpen your understanding.
🔹 Access Management Basics
How do you give a developer temporary access to S3 for 24 hours?
How do you allow EC2 to securely access S3 without using access keys?
A user can log in but still cannot access an S3 bucket. What would you check?
What’s the difference between inline and managed IAM policies, and when would you use each?
🔹 Security Best Practices
How do you enforce MFA for console and CLI access?
How do you restrict IAM users so they can log in only from your corporate IP range?
How do you enforce that all IAM users rotate access keys every 90 days?
How do you revoke IAM access immediately if a user leaves the company?
🔹 Cross-Account & Federation
How do you share access with another AWS account securely?
How do you grant cross-account access to Lambda functions?
How do you allow federated users from an Active Directory/SSO provider to log in?
🔹 Policy & Permission Control
What’s the best way to give read-only access to CloudWatch logs?
How do you ensure that developers can only launch specific EC2 instance types?
What are IAM permission boundaries, and when do you use them?
How do you implement least privilege across multiple teams?
🔹 Governance & Monitoring
How do you troubleshoot when an IAM policy denies access unexpectedly?
How do you prevent users from deleting important S3 objects?
A new intern needs limited console access. How do you configure it?
What’s the best way to assign permissions to hundreds of users at once?
How do you monitor and detect unusual IAM activity?
💡 IAM is one of the most critical topics in AWS interviews & real-world cloud security. Mastering these scenarios will set you apart.
